  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Find, in ascending powers of $a,$ the **first three terms** of the binomial expansion of ${(1-\\frac{3a}{4})}^{4}.$\n\n${(1-\\frac{3a}{4})}^{4}=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,+\\,\u22ef$",
  "worked_solution": "The first three terms of the binomial expansion for $(1+x)^{n}$ are given by\n\n$$\n{(1+x)}^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2!}{x}^{2}+\u22ef.\n$$\n\nBy substituting $x=-\\frac{3a}{4}$ and $n=4$ into the above formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1-\\frac{3a}{4})}^{4} & =1+4\\cdot (-\\frac{3a}{4})+\\frac{4(4-1)}{2!}\\cdot {(-\\frac{3a}{4})}^{2}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1-3a+\\frac{4\\cdot 3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{9{a}^{2}}{16}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1-3a+6\\cdot \\frac{9{a}^{2}}{16}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1-3a+\\frac{27}{8}{a}^{2}+\u22ef.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
